+**Pseudocode:**
+```python
+def platonic_solid_projection(mu, Sigma, solid_faces):
+    # solid_faces: list of tuples (phi_i, x_i, y_i, ripmap_grid) for i in 1..n
+    features = []
+    for phi_i, x_i, y_i, ripmap in solid_faces:
+        # Step 1 & 2: Construct projection matrix M_i (3x2)
+        M_i = np.column_stack((x_i, y_i))
+        # Step 3: Project mean (2x1) and covariance (2x2)
+        mu_proj = M_i.T @ mu
+        Sigma_proj = M_i.T @ Sigma @ M_i
+        # Step 4: Query feature vector
+        # Note: Interpolation and level-selection logic is defined in [Ripmap Encoding](8553-ripmap-encoding.md)
+        f_i = ripmap.query(mu_proj, Sigma_proj)
+        features.append(f_i)
+    # Step 5: Concatenate all feature vectors
+    return np.concatenate(features)
+```
 
